The schemas in protobuf/, and the FlatBuffers and Cap'n Proto schemas in
schema/, are generated from two COVESA specifications: the Vehicle Signal
Specification (https://github.com/COVESA/vehicle_signal_specification) and the
Vehicle Data Model (https://github.com/COVESA/vdm). Those specifications are
the property of COVESA and are subject to their own terms.

The generated schemas carry vocabulary, structure and documentation taken from
those specifications. The generator in sync/, and the decisions it encodes
about how that vocabulary maps onto AIP-shaped protobuf, are this
repository's own.

This product is built on protoc-gen-buffers
(https://github.com/the-protobuf-project/buffers) and follows the conventions
of protobuf-rfc (https://github.com/the-protobuf-project/protobuf-rfc), both
of which carry their own licences.
